# Local runtime / secrets — never commit
outbox/
logs/
reports/spool.db*
reports/*.lock*
reports/auth_broker_last.json
reports/desktop_cookie_inventory*.json
reports/auth_status_live.json
reports/chatgpt_send*.json
reports/*_probe*.json
reports/live_bridge_state.json
**/chatgpt_cookies.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw browser cookie DUMPS carry live session values — never commit (reports/ is NOT
# git-crypt'd). Encrypted stores live under cookie-store/ instead.
reports/*cdp_cookies*.json

# One-shot live-capture / audit dumps — regenerated by the auth + bus probes and carrying
# account/session identifiers. The durable narrative lives in the paired reports/*.md.
reports/auth_status_audit.json
reports/auth_watch_log.jsonl
reports/health_live.json
reports/*_last.*
reports/*_live_smoke_err.txt

# DENY-BY-DEFAULT for everything under reports/ except the human-written .md narratives.
#
# The name-by-name allowlist above fails OPEN: every new probe / audit / health dump is
# fully committable until someone remembers to add a line for it. MEASURED 2026-07-29 in a
# clean clone of main, with `git check-ignore --no-index` over the 85 paths present in a
# live crcp working tree: the allowlist did close all 85 of THOSE, but a merely-renamed
# dump was wide open — `reports/new_openai_audit_2026-08-01.json` and
# `reports/random_notes.json` were both committable. The class is genuinely sensitive: a
# count-only scan of the live dumps found a value-shaped `sk-…` string in
# reports/auth_status_audit.json (the other live dumps carried only the *field names*
# `access_token` / `refresh_token`, not values).
#
# Machine state lives in .json/.jsonl/.txt/.db; the durable narrative lives in .md. So deny
# the whole tree and re-admit only .md. Of the 59 tracked top-level reports, 47 are .md and
# 12 are .json — the .json stay tracked either way, because .gitignore never applies to an
# already-tracked path. A deliberate new dump can still be committed with `git add -f`.
#
# The directory negations are load-bearing: git will not descend into an ignored directory,
# so without them `!reports/**/*.md` would never be evaluated.
reports/**
!reports/
!reports/**/
!reports/**/*.md

# Runtime ingest drop-box (crcp/inbox.py consumes it) — payloads + cursor, never source.
inbox/

# GitHub trees-API scratch dumps used once to locate vendored upstream files (2 MB, regenerable).
vendor_src/**/tree.json

# Belt-and-braces for the cookie store: the .gitattributes git-crypt rule is inert unless
# `git-crypt unlock` has run on this box. Never let a plaintext cookie dump be staged.
cookie-store/*.json
